\newlabel{tab:msearch-rescue}{{6}{17}{Adaptive $M$-search rescue rates. ``Eligible'' is the number of pairs that missed at the default. ``Before'' and ``After'' are the domain-level Hit\% before and after the search. Labeled sweeps recover between $2.3$ and $16.7$~pp per domain; field-additivity sweeps recover more modestly because most pairs that were going to be rescued by $M$-change already were, and the remaining misses tend to be feature-specificity failures rather than overshoot failures.\relax }{table.caption.9}{}}
\newlabel{tab:msearch-rescue@cref}{{[table][6][2147483647]6}{[1][17][]17}}
